# Docker builds & warning hygiene

## How to build

- Prefer **Docker only** — do not install Node/Yarn/Rust/wasm-pack on the host unless the user asks.
- Dev image: `docker compose --profile development build hash-core-dev`
- Run: `docker compose --profile development up hash-core-dev` (port 3000 → 8080)
- Image target is `yarn-server` (`yarn serve:core`). Dockerfile builds `utils` + `engine-web` (WASM).

## What already works (keep working)

- WASM↔JS bridges use JSON round-trips in `packages/engine-web/rust/util.rs` (`to_js_value` / `from_js_value` via `serde_json` + `js_sys::JSON`). This matches historical `JsValue::from_serde` / `into_serde`.
- Do **not** use default `serde_wasm_bindgen::to_value` / `from_value`: Maps/`undefined` break the UI, and `from_value` mangles `AgentState` custom fields (symptoms: no agents, or `null.concat` in behaviors like `Multi_Ben_Or_Node.js`).
- `wasm-pack` is pinned in the Dockerfile to `0.15.0` via `cargo install`.
- `packages/engine-web/LICENSE.md` exists so wasm-pack stops complaining; Cargo `license` is `AGPL-3.0-only` (match package.json / root LICENSE). Do not set both `license` and `license-file`.
- Vendor `fux_kdtree` must keep **`edition = "2015"`**. `2018` breaks `use kdtree::...` paths. Visibility uses `pub(crate)` for private-module items.
- `docker-compose.yml` has **no** top-level `version:` (obsolete in Compose v2+).
- Yarn resolutions pin `@types/react` / `@types/react-dom` to 16.x; `tinygradient` is a direct core dependency for `gradient-path`.

## Intentionally left as warnings

Do not “fix” these without an explicit, tested plan:

| Warning | Why deferred |
|---|---|
| `vite-plugin-monaco-editor` wants `monaco-editor@>=0.33` (we pin `0.25.2`) | Broad API/worker/Jest surface; high UI regression risk |
| sanddance `fluentui-react-cdn-typings` wants `@types/react@16.9.34` | Peer noise vs our `16.9.56` resolution |
| `cypress-iframe` unmet `@types/cypress` | Stub package; Cypress ships its own types |
| `@deck.gl/layers` vs `@loaders.gl/core` peer | Upstream peer skew; core already uses `@loaders.gl/core: "*"` |

## Yarn lockfile

If `package.json` deps change, refresh `yarn.lock` **inside Docker** (frozen-lockfile builds will fail otherwise), e.g.:

```bash
docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/app -w /app node:20-bookworm bash -lc \
  'corepack enable && corepack prepare yarn@1.22.22 --activate && yarn install --ignore-scripts'
```
